.TH FILE_WRITE 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
file_write \- write bytes to a descriptor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.B long file_write(long descriptor, const char* buffer, long byte_count);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes bytes from buffer. Writes may be short and are not retried.
Supply a nonnegative byte count and sufficient buffer space.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns bytes written, or \-1 with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR file_open (3crunch),
.BR write (3crunch)
